                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16250644" author="kuaw26" created="Tue, 14 Nov 2017 01:36:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vsisko&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vsisko&quot;&gt;vsisko&lt;/a&gt; Could you take a look?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16250805" author="vsisko" created="Tue, 14 Nov 2017 04:09:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Visor does not show caches while cluster is not active.&lt;br/&gt;
Use &lt;b&gt;top -activate&lt;/b&gt; command for cluster activation.&lt;br/&gt;
After activation of cluster &lt;b&gt;cache&lt;/b&gt; command shows list of caches.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16251923" author="vkulichenko" created="Tue, 14 Nov 2017 18:43:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vsisko&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vsisko&quot;&gt;vsisko&lt;/a&gt;, got it. However, I find this a bit confusing. Why does Visor even show information in case cluster is inactive? Note that all API calls throw an exception in this case (&lt;tt&gt;Ignite#cacheNames&lt;/tt&gt; as well). I think Visor should clearly report this and also should be able to activate the cluster as well.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thoughts?&lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="16278193" author="vsisko" created="Tue, 5 Dec 2017 08:32:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Implemented showing of valid message on cache command when cluster in inactive.&lt;br/&gt;
Changed format of warning messages.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16279751" author="pkonstantinov" created="Wed, 6 Dec 2017 06:51:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Tested on branch&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16280481" author="kuaw26" created="Wed, 6 Dec 2017 16:49:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to master&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16321686" author="pkonstantinov" created="Thu, 11 Jan 2018 04:30:04 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Re-tested in master&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
